    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 3.9,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.99,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.93–0.95 from 5 h onward, which suggests reader saturation. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to test this. The 10x dilution read 0.361, which gives 3.6 when scaled. The 20x dilution read 0.170, which gives 3.4. The 50x dilution read 0.079, which gives 3.9. The scaled values are roughly consistent with each other, and the 50x value is the least affected by nonlinearity. Biomass at 18 h is therefore about 3.5–4 OD, roughly four times the undiluted reading of about 0.95. The plateau is a detector ceiling and not a real stationary phase at OD 0.93."
  },
